# Copy to .env and fill real values. NEVER commit real .env (gitignored).
#
# The harness talks to an OpenAI-compatible endpoint (the `openai` SDK), so the
# provider is just an env choice -- see src/harness/llm.py. Precedence:
# OPENAI_API_KEY wins if set, else GROQ_API_KEY. Set exactly one provider.

# --- Option A: OpenAI (recommended; paid credits, no free-tier daily cap, and
#     cleaner tool-calling than Llama). Just set the key + a model. ------------
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=            # optional; leave unset for api.openai.com
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini     # must support tool/function calling

# --- Option B: Groq (free tier, OpenAI-compatible). Note the free tier caps at
#     ~100k tokens/day, which a full defense-ladder sweep will exhaust. --------
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# GROQ_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
# GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile

# --- Optional overrides -----------------------------------------------------
# MODEL=                     # force one model id regardless of provider
# ATTACKER_MODEL=            # model for the adaptive iterative attacker
# GUARD_MODEL=               # model for the outbound_guard detector
